### USING GHIDRA TO DECOMPILE:
1. Download: https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/releases
2. Extract and run: ./ghidra_*/ghidraRun
3. File -> New Project, choose location and name
4. File -> Import File (select the level0 binary)
5. Click OK to start analysis, wait for completion
6. In Functions panel (left), search for "main"
7. Double-click "main" to view the function
8. Open Decompiler: Window -> Decompiler
9. C-like decompiled code appears in right panel

### COMMAND-LINE ALTERNATIVES:
Quick assembly view:
  objdump -d level0 | grep -A 100 "<main>:"

Interactive analysis (radare2):
  r2 level0       # Start radare2
  aa              # Analyze all
  s main          # Seek to main
  pdf             # Print disassembly
  pdc             # Print C-like code
  V               # Visual mode

Find hardcoded strings:
  strings level0 | grep -E "^[/a-zA-Z]"
  hexdump -C level0

